WEBVTT

00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,980
You know, anyone doing whole body hypothermia with success?

00:00:17,010 --> 00:00:18,770
Um, I don't.

00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:20,290
We've had patients over the years

00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:21,770
that have gone to Germany,

00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:24,170
because that's really the only place

00:00:24,170 --> 00:00:26,090
you could do a whole body hypothermia.

00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:28,730
There's some German cancer clinics.

00:00:28,730 --> 00:00:32,610
Now, quite honestly, I don't know how

00:00:32,610 --> 00:00:37,370
and how successful they've been

00:00:37,370 --> 00:00:39,530
and even keeping their doors open.

00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:43,930
Years ago, the choice of getting alternative cancer

00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:48,370
was to come to a clinic that was daring to step out

00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:50,570
like we were 20 years ago,

00:00:50,570 --> 00:00:51,850
doing what we were doing

00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:55,730
and we were being bombarded by the medical profession.

00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:58,930
There wasn't very many clinics in the United States

00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:03,930
as you know, one is there are now doing anything

00:01:05,430 --> 00:01:06,770
alternative in the United States.

00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:08,370
So in order to do something like

00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:10,490
if you looked at whole body hypothermia

00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:13,730
the German cancer clinics were very popular into that.

00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:17,410
The Mexico cancer clinics were not doing any whole body

00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,250
hypothermia.

00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:23,610
Um, really, I don't know if those German clinics

00:01:23,610 --> 00:01:24,650
are even still open.

00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:28,010
I know that German medical association has,

00:01:28,010 --> 00:01:31,890
you know, since COVID has gone much more Western.

00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:36,010
So I don't even know if those places still exist.

00:01:36,490 --> 00:01:39,930
And that's where people received this therapy

00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:40,530
in the past.

00:01:40,530 --> 00:01:42,570
I understand whole body hypothermia

00:01:42,570 --> 00:01:44,050
as you're going into this like,

00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:48,490
God, and you're, you're being, you have an IV tube in you

00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:50,930
and you're basically being completely sedated

00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:54,050
in order to do this because you're trying to get your,

00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:58,490
your core body temperature up to a fever state

00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:01,130
of a hundred, I do a hundred and seven.

00:02:01,130 --> 00:02:03,930
There's no way you would be able to tolerate that

00:02:03,930 --> 00:02:05,570
without being sedated.

00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:09,490
And that's for a long period of time anywhere between

00:02:09,490 --> 00:02:10,650
four to eight hours.

00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:14,850
It's just, it's a very intense and can be dangerous.

00:02:16,250 --> 00:02:17,730
There's no clinics in the US.

00:02:17,730 --> 00:02:20,890
There were, yeah, doing that to my knowledge,

00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:23,330
no clinics still that are doing anything like that.

00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:27,410
So I don't know of anybody who's done the whole body

00:02:27,410 --> 00:02:29,210
hypothermia and doing it currently.

